cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LatticeFlow Studio in your work, please cite it as below, and cite
  the methods it builds on (MACE, phonopy, spglib, ASE, pymatgen, the Materials
  Project); see the Acknowledgements section of the README.
title: LatticeFlow Studio
abstract: >-
  An interactive crystal and phonon studio: live forces from universal
  machine-learned interatomic potentials (MACE), relaxation, phonons, elastic
  tensors, convex hulls, a project library and a job queue, in the browser and
  from Python.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: switchfire6
repository-code: "https://github.com/switchfire6/latticeflow-studio"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
keywords:
  - materials science
  - phonons
  - machine-learning interatomic potentials
  - MACE
  - crystal structure
